Requirement coverage
The test cases above map to the PRD's major areas:

Authentication & validation: TC_LOGIN_001–020 — the PRD specifies email/password authentication, validation on blur, email-format validation, password-strength feedback, and authentication errors. 


UX & accessibility: TC_LOGIN_022–031 — auto-focus, clickable labels, loading states, responsive design, ARIA/keyboard support, high contrast, and themes are explicitly required. 


Security: TC_LOGIN_032–040 and TC_LOGIN_051–054 — HTTPS, encryption, secure sessions, rate limiting, SSO, and security/compliance requirements are specified. 


Performance & scalability: TC_LOGIN_044–046 and TC_LOGIN_055 — the PRD specifies sub-2-second loading, 99.9% availability, and support for thousands of simultaneous login attempts. 


Integration & user journey: TC_LOGIN_014, 037–043 and 047–049 — dashboard transition, analytics, support, SSO/social integrations, remembered credentials, and error recovery are covered. 


Note: Biometric authentication, adaptive authentication, PWA functionality, advanced personalization, and some analytics enhancements are explicitly listed as future enhancements in the PRD, so I have not treated them as current core-login test cases. 


